  "query_preview": "../Friday through Sunday/...An area of low pressure \nremains southwest of Haida Gwaii Friday allowing for showers to \ncontinue over the panhandle. Similar to what we have been seeing, \nthe highest rain totals and heaviest rates look to remain over \nsouthern areas. There is a chance for isolated thunderstorms to \ndevelop across on Friday shortwave moves over the area. Similar \nconditions will continue into Saturday as the low moves eastward \nallowing for some easterly flow to continue into SE AK. Although \nthere is signs of convection, confidence on thunderstorm development \nremains low at the moment. If thunderstorms do develop, periods of \ngusty winds and heavier rain are likely to occur. We will \ncontinue to monitor as we get closer to the weekend.\n\nAs the low pressure system moves eastward, an area of higher \npressure takes its place in the gulf. This could help to create \nslightly warmer weather for late in the week. This will also help to \ncreate drier weather for the end of the weekend. High temperatures \nare likely to reach into high 60s to the low to mid 70s. Warmest \nlocations look to be across the north where cloud cover will remain \nlower. As this higher pressure builds, it will also allow for winds \nover the gulf to become northwesterly for the weekend. Strongest \nwinds will be over the NE gulf into Icy Strait and Lynn Canal. \nOtherwise, overall winds remain on the lighter side, at or below 15 \nkts, for the long term forecast period.",
